    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "When I do `ci\"` using `mini.ai`, they will ignore escaped quote and treat them like the actual quote\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1c1e11cd-cbc2-4249-ac1d-81ade09b89e5\r\n\r\nAnd this is the vanilla `ci\"` (`nvim --clean`)\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f8c43998-8946-46cc-8b60-bce15b3ec858\r\n\r\nI also tried disabling `mini.ai`, and it work as intended\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n{\r\n  \"echasnovski/mini.nvim\",\r\n  version = \"*\",\r\n  config = function()\r\n    -- a/i textobjects\r\n    require(\"mini.ai\").setup()\r\n  end,\r\n}\r\n```",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">When I do <code class=\"notranslate\">ci\"</code> using <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.ai</code>, they will ignore escaped quote and treat them like the actual quote</p>\n<details open=\"\" class=\"details-reset border rounded-2\">\n  <summary class=\"tmp-px-3 py-2\">\n    <svg aria-hidden=\"true\" data-component=\"Octicon\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" data-view-component=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-device-camera-video\">\n    <path d=\"M16 3.75v8.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.136.643L11 10.575v.675A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 9.25 13h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 11.25v-6.5C0 3.784.784 3 1.75 3h7.5c.966 0 1.75.784 1.75 1.75v.675l3.864-2.318A.75.75 0 0 1 16 3.75Zm-6.5 1a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25h-7.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v6.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-6.5ZM11 8.825l3.5 2.1v-5.85l-3.5 2.1Z\"></path>\n</svg>\n    <span class=\"m-1\">Screen.Recording.2024-10-02.113759.mp4</span>\n    <span class=\"dropdown-caret\"></span>\n  </summary>\n\n  <video src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/57800056/372730292-1c1e11cd-cbc2-4249-ac1d-81ade09b89e5.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..fGzEgBaiMmQGkaZSFapp33cwK1czlzUe3g9qyGzp8MU\" data-canonical-src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/57800056/372730292-1c1e11cd-cbc2-4249-ac1d-81ade09b89e5.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..fGzEgBaiMmQGkaZSFapp33cwK1czlzUe3g9qyGzp8MU\" controls=\"controls\" muted=\"muted\" class=\"d-block rounded-bottom-2 border-top width-fit\" style=\"max-height:640px; min-height: 200px\">\n\n  </video>\n</details>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">And this is the vanilla <code class=\"notranslate\">ci\"</code> (<code class=\"notranslate\">nvim --clean</code>)</p>\n<details open=\"\" class=\"details-reset border rounded-2\">\n  <summary class=\"tmp-px-3 py-2\">\n    <svg aria-hidden=\"true\" data-component=\"Octicon\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" data-view-component=\"true\" class=\"octicon octicon-device-camera-video\">\n    <path d=\"M16 3.75v8.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.136.643L11 10.575v.675A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 9.25 13h-7.5A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 0 11.25v-6.5C0 3.784.784 3 1.75 3h7.5c.966 0 1.75.784 1.75 1.75v.675l3.864-2.318A.75.75 0 0 1 16 3.75Zm-6.5 1a.25.25 0 0 0-.25-.25h-7.5a.25.25 0 0 0-.25.25v6.5c0 .138.112.25.25.25h7.5a.25.25 0 0 0 .25-.25v-6.5ZM11 8.825l3.5 2.1v-5.85l-3.5 2.1Z\"></path>\n</svg>\n    <span class=\"m-1\">Screen.Recording.2024-10-02.113918.mp4</span>\n    <span class=\"dropdown-caret\"></span>\n  </summary>\n\n  <video src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/57800056/372730594-f8c43998-8946-46cc-8b60-bce15b3ec858.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..oxHBS78JbOEe2-0Nqi-KtHLG7lFXHn6gxrYDgaAq-dI\" data-canonical-src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/57800056/372730594-f8c43998-8946-46cc-8b60-bce15b3ec858.mp4?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..oxHBS78JbOEe2-0Nqi-KtHLG7lFXHn6gxrYDgaAq-dI\" controls=\"controls\" muted=\"muted\" class=\"d-block rounded-bottom-2 border-top width-fit\" style=\"max-height:640px; min-height: 200px\">\n\n  </video>\n</details>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">I also tried disabling <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.ai</code>, and it work as intended</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"{\n  &quot;echasnovski/mini.nvim&quot;,\n  version = &quot;*&quot;,\n  config = function()\n    -- a/i textobjects\n    require(&quot;mini.ai&quot;).setup()\n  end,\n}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\">{\n  <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>echasnovski/mini.nvim<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">version</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>*<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,\n  <span class=\"pl-en\">config</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>()\n    <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">--</span> a/i textobjects</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>(<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.ai<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>).<span class=\"pl-c1\">setup</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n}</pre></div>",
    "bodyText": "When I do ci\" using mini.ai, they will ignore escaped quote and treat them like the actual quote\n\n  \n    \n    \n\n    Screen.Recording.2024-10-02.113759.mp4\n    \n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n\nAnd this is the vanilla ci\" (nvim --clean)\n\n  \n    \n    \n\n    Screen.Recording.2024-10-02.113918.mp4\n    \n  \n\n  \n\n  \n\n\nI also tried disabling mini.ai, and it work as intended\n{\n  \"echasnovski/mini.nvim\",\n  version = \"*\",\n  config = function()\n    -- a/i textobjects\n    require(\"mini.ai\").setup()\n  end,\n}",
