    "closed": true,
    "closedAt": "2024-10-02T07:48:25Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, I am afraid this is how 'mini.ai' works: it treats any `\"` as a valid `\"` (and tries to find [balanced quotes](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/848c5e8f428faf843051768e0d56104cd02aea1f/doc/mini-ai.txt#L23), for that matter). This decision is mostly due to a combination of willing to have a more consistent behavior across all built-in textobjects and Lua patterns implementation details (in particular relying on `%bxy` balanced pattern).\r\n\r\nIf you want the built-in behavior for `\"` and don't mind loosing the \"next\"/\"prev\" forced search methods together with consecutive application in Visual mode, you can disable 'mini.ai' only for `\"` [by setting it to `false` in `config.custom_textobjects`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/848c5e8f428faf843051768e0d56104cd02aea1f/doc/mini-ai.txt#L479-L480).",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, I am afraid this is how 'mini.ai' works: it treats any <code class=\"notranslate\">\"</code> as a valid <code class=\"notranslate\">\"</code> (and tries to find <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/848c5e8f428faf843051768e0d56104cd02aea1f/doc/mini-ai.txt#L23\">balanced quotes</a>, for that matter). This decision is mostly due to a combination of willing to have a more consistent behavior across all built-in textobjects and Lua patterns implementation details (in particular relying on <code class=\"notranslate\">%bxy</code> balanced pattern).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If you want the built-in behavior for <code class=\"notranslate\">\"</code> and don't mind loosing the \"next\"/\"prev\" forced search methods together with consecutive application in Visual mode, you can disable 'mini.ai' only for <code class=\"notranslate\">\"</code> <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/848c5e8f428faf843051768e0d56104cd02aea1f/doc/mini-ai.txt#L479-L480\">by setting it to <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code> in <code class=\"notranslate\">config.custom_textobjects</code></a>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Yes, I am afraid this is how 'mini.ai' works: it treats any \" as a valid \" (and tries to find balanced quotes, for that matter). This decision is mostly due to a combination of willing to have a more consistent behavior across all built-in textobjects and Lua patterns implementation details (in particular relying on %bxy balanced pattern).\nIf you want the built-in behavior for \" and don't mind loosing the \"next\"/\"prev\" forced search methods together with consecutive application in Visual mode, you can disable 'mini.ai' only for \" by setting it to false in config.custom_textobjects.",
